      "default": "Spongiotic",
      "help": "The pattern sets the diagnosis list and the features offered. Graft-versus-host disease opens its own grading.",
      "reference": {
        "title": "Reaction patterns",
        "intro": "Choose the dominant pattern at scanning power; the diagnosis list and the features follow it.",
        "groups": [
          {
            "heading": "Epidermal and junctional",
            "points": [
              "Spongiotic: intercellular oedema in the epidermis, from slight widening of the spaces to vesicles",
              "Psoriasiform: elongated rete ridges, regular (psoriasis) or irregular (lichen simplex chronicus)",
              "Interface (vacuolar): vacuoles and apoptotic keratinocytes along the basal layer with a sparse infiltrate",
              "Interface (lichenoid): a band of lymphocytes in the papillary dermis that obscures the junction"
            ],
            "images": []
          },
          {
            "heading": "Dermal and subcutaneous",
            "points": [
              "Perivascular: lymphocytes around superficial, or superficial and deep, vessels with little epidermal change",
              "Vasculitis: inflammatory cells in vessel walls with fibrinoid necrosis; leukocytoclasia and red cells in small-vessel disease",
              "Vesiculobullous: the level of the split and the cells in the blister; direct immunofluorescence classifies the autoimmune diseases",
              "Granulomatous: sarcoidal, palisading, interstitial, tuberculoid, suppurative or foreign body",
              "Panniculitis: septal or lobular, with or without vasculitis",
              "Sclerosing: thickened dermal collagen and loss of periadnexal fat, or a homogenised papillary dermis"
            ],
            "images": []
          }
        ]
      }
    },
